A freestanding wasm32 build of the C runtime template (bend2/comp.ts),
for plain clang --target=wasm32 -nostdlib with wasm-ld and no emcc
(bend-wasm's tools/clang-wasm/build.sh, TODO t-fwjpak4c steps B and C).
All of it is under one guard, BEND_WASM_FREESTANDING; without it the C is
the same as before, so native and emcc builds do not change.

- The guard defines __EMSCRIPTEN__ before the includes, so the build takes
  patch 0002's wasm path as it is (two-word Env through musttail, WL_ROOM,
  static corpus and Term stack, one worker, refused effects); it is an
  error under emcc, whose target predefines it.
- No libc is linked: the sysroot's headers declare, and a Freestanding
  section after the includes defines what the runtime calls (bend-wasm's
  docs/clang-wasm.md lists it): mem* as memory.copy/memory.fill (bulk
  memory required), the string functions, strtol and atoi; malloc,
  calloc, realloc and free over __heap_base and memory.grow, for the host
  side only (a failure stays "bend: host allocation failed"); unbuffered
  stdout and stderr and a printf of the runtime's formats; no-op locks of
  the one worker, and traps where only a second thread or a parked request
  could lead (pthread_cond_wait, the wake pipe's read, select).
- The host's part is named imports of one module, "bend": write(fd, data,
  len), exit(code) and now() (monotonic ns). The math functions the
  emitter can call, strtof, strtod and the formatter of %e and %f
  (bend_fmt_fp, which this patch declares) come from musl sources the
  build links (bend-wasm's tools/clang-wasm/musl, step C), never from the
  host.

Retired by: an upstream freestanding wasm target of Bend's C runtime
(https://github.com/bendlang/bend/issues/1598).

